  "guideHowSentenceTitle": "Read today's sentence",
  "guideHowSentenceStep1": "Open the Learn tab to see today's sentence. Sentences come in sets of five, and the header shows how far along you are.",
  "guideHowSentenceStep3": "Gold words are the ones you're learning. The quiz asks about those.",
  "guideHowSentenceStep4": "Tap the sentence card to open the detail screen.",
  "guideHowDetailTitle": "The detail screen",
  "guideHowDetailLead": "The detail screen explains Thai sentences in more depth. The more clues you have — situation, style, spelling and tone — the better that word stays in memory.",
  "guideHowSoundTitle": "Listen and say it aloud",
  "guideHowSoundStep1": "“Listen to the model” plays the audio of the Thai sentence on a loop.",
  "guideHowSoundStep2": "In “Pronunciation practice” on the detail screen, hold down the “Hold to speak” button and read along, and it judges on the spot whether your tones match.",
  "guideHowSoundStep3": "In pronunciation practice, green means correct, amber means close, and red means wrong. Tap a word to see the model's curve against your own, and how to fix it.",
  "guideHowQuizTitle": "Take the check quiz",
  "guideHowQuizStep1": "“Check if it stuck” below the sentence takes you to the check quiz.",
  "guideHowQuizStep2": "You choose the meaning of the target word (the gold one) from the sentence you just read, out of four options.",
  "guideHowQuizStep3": "Once you answer, an explanation of that word's meaning and usage appears.",
  "guideHowQuizStep4": "From the results screen, go on to the next sentence. After you finish the fifth, you flow straight into the summary quiz.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizTitle": "Take the summary quiz",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep1": "A milestone quiz that comes every time you finish five sentences. From the sentences you've studied, you choose the word that goes in the blank.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep2": "The sentences it asks about are chosen with gaps in between — the day before, three days ago, a week ago, and so on. Within those, words you haven't got down yet come first.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep3": "You can use hints. Press once for the pronunciation, again for the translation. Once you're used to it, answering without hints makes your vocabulary score grow faster.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep4": "If you're unsure, “Check the sentence” takes you back to the sentence.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep5": "Correct answers here are what's reflected in your vocabulary score.",
  "guideHowSettingsTitle": "What you can do in Settings",
  "guideHowSettingsStep1": "Change your notification time, the display font, and the language of translations and explanations.",
  "guideHowSettingsStep2": "You can also open the topic selection for your next sentence and the ranking from here.",
  "guideHowSettingsStep3": "You can open this guide any time from “How-to guide” in Settings."
